{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1336104-help-with-time","id":1336104,"title":"Help with Time","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-16T15:24:12-07:00","id":1336104,"title":"Help with Time","content":"I'm having trouble wrapping my head around how the Time arcanum will make a Consilium and the Awakened world in general look. Any given Consilium seems likely to have at least one or two Masters of Time for whom messing with the recent past wouldn't be difficult. In such an environment how could the members of a Consilium be threatened short of some sort of large scale invasion?<br /> <br /> Say a banisher or the Seers kill a member of the Consilium. It would be almost trivial, given my current understanding of how Time magic works, for a Master of Time to get a warning back to the past. <br /> <br /> OK, maybe that's not 100% to save the individual. But it doesn't really need to be for the sake of my question. In many cases being warned in this way (if not having the situation intervened with more directly) would be enough for there to be profound impact on what happened.<br /> <br /> Given that, shouldn't a Consilium essentially never be surprised? Wouldn't a Consilium with at least one or two Time Masters (maybe being compensated with resources, Mysteries, etc), which is to say what I think would be almost all Consilia, look like Minority Report's world with precrime? <br /> <br /> Council sitting around a desk:<br /> &quot;Well Mage1, you came back from a week in the future to warn us that EventA will happen and two mages will die.&quot;<br /> &quot;OK, I'll let the sentinels know and they'll make some wellness checks and try to divert this.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if this doesn't prevent the disaster every time, I don't know why the attempt wouldn't be made.<br /> <br /> My trouble is I don't know why this wouldn't be the norm in almost every Consilium for nearly every major incident. I'd appreciate some help with this and maybe with the use of Time in general in the context of a Consilium.<br /> <br /> I ask as someone in the early stages of prepping my first Mage 2e chronicle. Both out of simple curiosity, and so I have a more concrete understanding with which to provide an answer if one of my players asks (and one of them will likely be doing a fair bit of Time stuff themselves).<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25031,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","user":"NitroXanax","date":". 09-16-2019, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","name":"NitroXanax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T16:15:40-07:00","id":1336111,"title":"","content":"A Consilium is a common-law court for mediating disputes between individual mages, who are largely concerned with their own business and their relations with each other where relevant to those interests, which are not necessarily helped by taking time out of their day to avert a murder.<br /> <br /> Time travel that accomplishes anything changes the events of the past using the resources available at the time, which the basic facts of opportunity cost render as &quot;anything you tap to prevent that murder prevents it from being used the way it was used originally.&quot;<br /> <br /> Time travel that is in the process of accomplishing anything is discernible to any mage with baseline competence in the Arcanum who is using it to examine the world around them, which freely includes all Acanthus and any member of a Time-based Legacy.<br /> <br /> A Consilium acting in the way you describe does not just have to compensate the Master whose magic is necessary for the trip, it has to account for <i>every other mage that trip interferes with</i> as well as any effect it has on the Mysteries they're studying, and that's if nobody in the loop is invested in seeing the established present continue to be as it is.<br /> <br /> The far-more-widespread prevalence of actual precognition is the greater concern as far as the actual running of the setting, because that doesn't rely on convincing one of the most powerful people in the area to kick the butterfly's nest for favors or personal investment.<br /> <br /> Wisdom is generally going to indicate that the drastic one-shot-at-a-time nature of time travel is best handled delicately and infrequently. Power politics and the nature of obsession mean Masters seldom get to where they are by being too concerned about every other fellow reality-warper in their area, particularly if it cuts into their studies for someone they don't particularly care about.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling with the particulars here because you're also conflating &quot;Consilium-threatening disaster&quot; and &quot;Minority Report-style pre-crime&quot; despite the tremendous difference in scale between those two. Are you asking how bad things can ever happen in a territory occupied by mages or are you asking if city-shaking events can retain their impact in the face of Time Mastery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T16:23:09-07:00","id":1336113,"title":"","content":"So, the first and always important thing to consider is Cornelius's Lament, which needs to be featured in the books sometime: &quot;The trouble is, the other side can do magic too, Prime Minister.&quot; That includes Time.<br /> <br /> The second and always important thing to consider is that mages are assholes, here read as &quot;the more a mage becomes more of a mage, the more their own pursuits take precedence over the affairs of others, and the nature of state becomes more a convienence rather than a community.&quot; Basically, a Master of an Arcanum is usually no longer as invested in their own Consilium/Assembly as they are their own cabal, if not their own personal interests, and as such a Consilium has to invest more in them for their resources. Among Seers, this problem is exacerbated.<br /> <br /> A third and related point is that a Consilium or Assembly may not be as much of a point of interest as a general Caucus, if those maintain their interest. This exacerbates the problem of getting a master of an Arcanum to dedicate their resources to the area on the whole.<br /> <br /> A fourth point is that the inherent structure of practices amongst all the Arcana means that a mage has a myriad of options for concealing or defending their own effects long before they learn the Art of Breaking Shit, which usually means that any decent practitioner of Doing Shady Things is more easily equipped than the number of practitioners who can Do Really Complex And Metaphysically Raw Shit.<br /> <br /> A fifth point is that few mages go at commiting actions against the will of the community rarely do so with straight forward means according the common understanding of magic. Such mages tend to employ something Mysterious to tangle the weave that makes it harder to just act against.<br /> <br /> I mean, it really all comes down to a) offenders also have magic, b) powerful mages have better things to do that invest super heavily into their community, and c) no one takes a straight shot at a mage community outside of stupid/exceptional circumstances.<br /> <br /> A lot of &quot;Why doesn't X happen when Mages are So Versatile/Powerful&quot; comes down to those big three ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T16:36:26-07:00","id":1336115,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, when it comes to mages vs. mages, the advantage is going to go to whichever side actually did the thing in the past. Time travelers are very obvious to other mages with Time, making them easy targets. It's only a Time 2 spell to shield a subject from time traveling interference, or to shield someone from being observed with Time magic. And of course, something like changing the death of a person has very weak temporal sympathy to contend with when it comes to warning themselves about stuff.<br /> <br /> So, like lots of things with Mage, it's not that a Consilium wouldn't have Time Masters and they wouldn't use their powers for the good of their fellows (though Mages tend not to be the most altruistic types....). It's just that trying to rely too much on one trick is the path to hubris. Enemy mages can muck with time too, and getting into a time travel war is not something most mages would be interested in.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T16:36:50-07:00","id":1336116,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, sixth point: It doesn't matter how many Masters of Time there are, there are a lot more Disciples of Time in some form or fashion than there are them, and some point you can't be arsed to bother with all of the pings.<br /> <br /> And seventh point: While certainly the potency of a Master is not to be ignored, there's an overestimation of how powerful on a broader scale a Master is going to be. We aren't talking about Archmages here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T17:34:15-07:00","id":1336122,"title":"","content":"Thanks to everyone for responding as thoughtfully as you have. I'm on my phone so it's difficult to quote you for specific replies but I'll do my best to respond to the common threads for now.<br /> <br /> One is that mages, Masters especially, might not be interested in interfering in these matters. Reading through the Order books I have (which are admittedly for 1e) the positions which are described as being occupied by Masters also seem to be described as being generally interested in the goings on of their Orders (and I believe most mages are in an order, with apostates being rare). Am I misunderstanding the costs and consequences for using Time magic in the way I've described? If so that's likely what I need assistance with. Let's say there's a player in my group who is a Master of Time and a member of his cabal dies. It could be a car crash or a nasty spirit encounter or an experiment gone wrong. That player is likely to want to use Time to get a warning back to the past - his work could end there. The cabalmate in question can now begin to take precautions. And this would all be extremely easy for that Time mage. A single spell he might cast in an hour. Why might an NPC mage not behave similarly? Even toward non-cabalmates? Are there reasons the player doing it would be ill advised?<br /> <br /> <br /> Another point has been that the other mages have magic, too. That I'm on board with. I get that in a conflict between groups of mages it's gonna get crazy. I'm more talking about smaller scale scenarios. If I'm a banisher or a murderous ephemeral entity say, am I a real danger to anyone in a Consilium? Even if I kill someone, assuming other mages do get involved that person dying seems likely to be undone. I'm not referring to consequences suffered by the antagonist, I'm more referring to their ability to deal lasting harm to anyone in a real way. That again assumes an interested Time Master willing to overlook whatever consequences I might not be considering from my first point. <br /> <br /> I guess my ultimate question is whether mages who are part of a Consilium with interested Time Masters are going to be immune from lethal dangers from anything short of a large scale Seer assault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25031,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","user":"NitroXanax","date":". 09-16-2019, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","name":"NitroXanax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T17:55:00-07:00","id":1336129,"title":"","content":"Is it an issue of hubris? THAT could make a lot of sense to me, if it's the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","name":"NitroXanax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T20:48:07-07:00","id":1336147,"title":"","content":"As people have already said, you overestimate how much Mages care for one another. They will mobilize to hunt down a common threat (like a banisher) but effectively bringing someone back from the dead is way too much trouble for most Mages to bother with.<br /> <br /> Just for reference, check out in Signs of Sorcery the guidelines for using Status to get a Spell cast. Yeah, maybe sometimes they would do it, but those would be stand out moments","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","user":"EW-Matias","date":". 09-16-2019, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T21:27:07-07:00","id":1336149,"title":"","content":"A Mage with a Master of Time in their cabal is the most likely to be saved by said Master. Everyone else is likely to be on their own for the most part.<br /> <br /> To your question about high ranking Order members, like Masters, actually most of them fuck off to contemplate the \u201cdeep\u201d Mysteries, and usually cannot be bothered to act on anything less than their own personal interests or something that truly threatens their Caucus.<br /> <br /> And most uses of magic aren\u2019t trivial. Especially time magic because it means you have to go change somebody\u2019s timeline. If you do it yourself, well, that\u2019s time not spent getting the best bang for your buck for your personal benefit probably. If you change someone else\u2019s then you probably also have to decide if you want to protect yourself from the changes or not, and you have no way of monitoring or modifying whatever shenanigans your agent gets up to when they\u2019re back there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T21:50:21-07:00","id":1336150,"title":"","content":"The Art is self-expression for the Awakened \u2014 the spells they cast inform their magical personas in ways that have an impact on how the world responds to them in the longer term through their Long-Term Nimbus and other subtle pressures, so &quot;hey, mystically align yourself with this crisis in a way that could snowball badly if not treated with care&quot; is a suggestion that's going to be met with some resistance by all but the most impulsive without some personal stake to shorten the distance for them.<br /> <br /> Mages tend to be a little more invested in their Orders than other mages in the area because that's where most of their teachers, students, and direct contacts come from \u2014 mages train and are trained by other mages, and while Legacies are the most direct about this relationship there is a reason the Sects serve as readily to ground a mage's understanding of their foundational principles as Paths do.<br /> <br /> Remember also that time travel isn't a fire-and-forget thing \u2014 spending an hour to cast Corridors of Time is just the start of the process of reliving the spell's Duration in time from the jump point, after which you skip forward the rest of the way to the present and may well discover that nothing meaningfully changed and you have to do it all over again. Master-level spells tend to be factor-intensive even without their limited Reach, and there's a reason the Path with the best understanding of Time is also the one primed to think in terms of consequences, weight, and precision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T23:43:48-07:00","id":1336157,"title":"","content":"&quot;Who died? The weasel face kid who keeps messing up my domino study? OH! Oh, no, you mean the apprentice of that self-righteous prat. <i>Sure</i>, I'll consider it, once he returns my grimoire and brings that book he promised on over. Oh, and you'll owe me lunch. I enjoy our chats.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T00:29:58-07:00","id":1336158,"title":"","content":"Consider that consilium have a trading favors economy.<br /> A master of time could cast the spell to save a hierarch for free, but most of the time the victims are low caliber mages.<br /> In those cases the master would have full right to require high value services for his casting.<br /> But, given the nature of time magic, the master must ask for payment during or after the time travel, or it will be undone!<br /> And the saved mage could say that the master is telling a lie only to get the advantage, because he could give evidence of the death only using magic.<br /> So both mages must trust each other and the victim must have something interesting for the master, because the master rarely would be so altruistic to take all this effort and risks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T00:58:15-07:00","id":1336161,"title":"","content":"Oh, and there is also the fact that if the enemies of the consilium ever know what the master can do it would become a primary target, so the price required for the spell will probably consider that risk.<br /> And also the spell, if not casted in a demesne, would require a lot of mana to not risk paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T01:06:00-07:00","id":1336163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1336104-help-with-time?p=1336158#post1336158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider that consilium have a trading favors economy.<br /> A master of time could cast the spell to save a hierarch for free, but most of the time the victims are low caliber mages.<br /> In those cases the master would have full right to require high value services for his casting.<br /> But, given the nature of time magic, the master must ask for payment during or after the time travel, or it will be undone!<br /> And the saved mage could say that the master is telling a lie only to get the advantage, because he could give evidence of the death only using magic.<br /> So both mages must trust each other and the victim must have something interesting for the master, because the master rarely would be so altruistic to take all this effort and risks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That problem is resolved with the use of High Speech.<br /> You are not credible ( chance die), when lie with the Magic Language.<br /> Or the use of Words of Truth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T02:14:28-07:00","id":1336170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1336104-help-with-time?p=1336163#post1336163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That problem is resolved with the use of High Speech.<br /> You are not credible ( chance die), when lie with the Magic Language.<br /> Or the use of Words of Truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don t considered those options, my bad.<br /> But as a Master of time i would still ask very high prices like:<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course i can save your cabal mate, if you bring to me:<br /> -a Mastigos soul stone<br /> -an Eidoform coin Artifact<br /> -20 Mana<br /> -and your cabal will support my law proposal on the next consilium meeting<br /> AND remember, if you ever upset me in the future i ll go back before this moment and write a note for me to do not help you.<br /> Seems a fair price to me, no?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T06:03:15-07:00","id":1336189,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25031\" data-vbnamecard=\"25031\">NitroXanax</a> Something to take into consideration is the changes to the setting from 1e to 2e. The first edition books gave a setting where the consilium's mages were basically bound to help each other in order to keep a united front, though a varying amount of squabbling and even fighting would still occur. 2e has gone to pretty decent lengths to rewrite the consilium as a force tied to one very specific idea: keep mages from killing each other. There's plenty of wiggle room within that for people claiming authority and/or responsibility. However, at the end of the day the leaders of the consilium are mostly judges and police, not fire fighters and EMTs.<br /> <br /> Now, you could make a legitimate argument that the makers of the game and far too many of its fans have a jaded view of the world when it comes to interpersonal relationships (and the world in general) and that it's overly affecting their perception of the setting. I personally get that vibe all the time. However, we ARE also talking about the Chronicles of Darkness world here. Most people there are jerks just because. If that doesn't suit you then by all means, please change it at your table. However, if you don't then you'll need to keep that in mind when trying to understand why certain things don't happen in the setting: so long as it requires human effort there's going to be any number of dozens of personal reasons why any given mage won't get off their ass to help another person (mage or not).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T11:33:18-07:00","id":1336252,"title":"","content":"It definitely seems the case that the disconnect was in how I viewed the mages as people. With them doing things like, for example: Maintaining cults to guide sleepers toward Awakening. Or gathering into Orders that seem to have pretty altruistic goals (with apostates, the ones I'd considered the most likely to adopt the &quot;lonely hermit who doesn't care about the wider Awakened community&quot; mentality, being described as rare). With that view of the Awakened I considered it strange that they wouldn't step in to help when another Pentacle/Diamond mage died. Especially given how serious I thought the Pentacle v Seers conflict to be. I figured in light of that they might take a &quot;no man is an island - it tolls for thee&quot; attitude toward their peers. So they want to guide sleepers toward Awakening but don't seem to care much what happens to them once they're mages? I guess I need to grimdark my setting a bit more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","name":"NitroXanax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:02:19-07:00","id":1336265,"title":"","content":"&quot;The wider Awakened community&quot; is your teachers, your students, your cabal, and people you owe or are owed by in your capacity as a magical actor \u2014 they seldom exist in a vacuum, but that doesn't make stepping in on their self-determination the first impulse of an established wizard. These aren't your next-door neighbors and little cousins, they're your students and your peers in largely independent study who happen to be in the same city as you are when you're all wearing your Shadow Names. There's territorial disputes involved in this process as readily as delicate negotiations over resources.<br /> <br /> The Sects in general understand the Arcana in fashions steered by the perspectives of their focal Paths, so the Moros inform the view of Death as not a thing to be unduly avoided and the Acanthus recognize that fucking around with Time is a recipe for trouble if you're not very careful and the Mastigos can tell you for free that your sympathetic connections being &quot;weaknesses&quot; is no excuse to cut them out of your life. Collections of lore and students are called Legacies for a reason.<br /> <br /> The Orders having well-meaning goals doesn't change their Wisdom-affecting views of what magic is for, and &quot;guide Sleepers toward Awakening&quot; is notably most strongly held as a conviction by the same institution that thinks hubris is a coward's word and therefore has a well-established habit of self-destructing from ill-advised use of magic.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;once they're mages&quot; they're either a different kind of resource or they're competitors for assets. You can be invested in their well-being if you're so inclined, but there's a thick line between &quot;I care about the well-being of my local brain surgeon&quot; and &quot;I will warp history so that my local brain surgeon \u2014 who knows enough to ask about upcoming crises and can call in favors from people who aren't me \u2014 survives his own failure of preparation even though my area of specialty has no need for brain surgery.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;grimdark&quot; for characters defined by personal obsession with the supernatural, who operate within constructed magical identities often substantially divorced from their mundane lives, who attract supernatural complications to that identity at the bare minimum and mostly only use magic as a deliberate act, to have a live-and-let-live approach to bad things happening to other such characters in the neighboring vicinity of their agreed-upon allotment of mystical real estate in the local cooperatively-enforced justice system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:10:12-07:00","id":1336272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NitroXanax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1336104-help-with-time?p=1336252#post1336252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It definitely seems the case that the disconnect was in how I viewed the mages as people. With them doing things like, for example: Maintaining cults to guide sleepers toward Awakening. Or gathering into Orders that seem to have pretty altruistic goals (with apostates, the ones I'd considered the most likely to adopt the &amp;quot;lonely hermit who doesn't care about the wider Awakened community&amp;quot; mentality, being described as rare). With that view of the Awakened I considered it strange that they wouldn't step in to help when another Pentacle/Diamond mage died. Especially given how serious I thought the Pentacle v Seers conflict to be. I figured in light of that they might take a &amp;quot;no man is an island - it tolls for thee&amp;quot; attitude toward their peers. So they want to guide sleepers toward Awakening but don't seem to care much what happens to them once they're mages? I guess I need to grimdark my setting a bit more!</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course in a situation of harsh conflict vs seer the teamwork attitude would be a little better.<br /> That said remember that chronicle of darkness tells stories about monsters, and mages are not hideus but they are still monsters corrupted by power and hubris.<br /> Surely every monster has both bright and dark sides, just like normal humans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:16:24-07:00","id":1336275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1336104-help-with-time?p=1336265#post1336265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The wider Awakened community&quot; is your teachers, your students, your cabal, and people you owe or are owed by in your capacity as a magical actor \u2014 they seldom exist in a vacuum, but that doesn't make stepping in on their self-determination the first impulse of an established wizard. These aren't your next-door neighbors and little cousins, they're your students and your peers in largely independent study who happen to be in the same city as you are when you're all wearing your Shadow Names. There's territorial disputes involved in this process as readily as delicate negotiations over resources.<br /> <br /> The Sects in general understand the Arcana in fashions steered by the perspectives of their focal Paths, so the Moros inform the view of Death as not a thing to be unduly avoided and the Acanthus recognize that fucking around with Time is a recipe for trouble if you're not very careful and the Mastigos can tell you for free that your sympathetic connections being &quot;weaknesses&quot; is no excuse to cut them out of your life. Collections of lore and students are called Legacies for a reason.<br /> <br /> The Orders having well-meaning goals doesn't change their Wisdom-affecting views of what magic is for, and &quot;guide Sleepers toward Awakening&quot; is notably most strongly held as a conviction by the same institution that thinks hubris is a coward's word and therefore has a well-established habit of self-destructing from ill-advised use of magic.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;once they're mages&quot; they're either a different kind of resource or they're competitors for assets. You can be invested in their well-being if you're so inclined, but there's a thick line between &quot;I care about the well-being of my local brain surgeon&quot; and &quot;I will warp history so that my local brain surgeon \u2014 who knows enough to ask about upcoming crises and can call in favors from people who aren't me \u2014 survives his own failure of preparation even though my area of specialty has no need for brain surgery.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;grimdark&quot; for characters defined by personal obsession with the supernatural, who operate within constructed magical identities often substantially divorced from their mundane lives, who attract supernatural complications to that identity at the bare minimum and mostly only use magic as a deliberate act, to have a live-and-let-live approach to bad things happening to other such characters in the neighboring vicinity of their agreed-upon allotment of mystical real estate in the local cooperatively-enforced justice system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm on board with what you're telling me.<br /> <br /> What is going to be the most common primary motivation for an individual Guardian or Silver Ladder maintaining a Labyrinth or Cryptopoly and guiding sleepers to Awaken if the resulting mages are going to be viewed as competitors? Is it the resources and influence that running a mystery cult provides and the Awakenings are more incidental? Is there an expectation that the new mages who develop within these cults are going to be the students of the same individuals (and not other people within the Order, maybe) running them? Or are the specific people running these cults likely to just be following the orders of their caucus leaders? This is a genuine question, not trying to play a semantic game with anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25031-nitroxanax","name":"NitroXanax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T12:38:52-07:00","id":1336284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NitroXanax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1336104-help-with-time?p=1336275#post1336275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is going to be the most common primary motivation for an individual Guardian or Silver Ladder maintaining a Labyrinth or Cryptopoly and guiding sleepers to Awaken if the resulting mages are going to be viewed as competitors? Is it the resources and influence that running a mystery cult provides and the Awakenings are more incidental? Is there an expectation that the new mages who develop within these cults are going to be the students of the same individuals (and not other people within the Order, maybe) running them? Or are the specific people running these cults likely to just be following the orders of their caucus leaders? This is a genuine question, not trying to play a semantic game with anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Guardians' case, at least, most mages the Labyrinth turns out go to other Orders due to a combination of their not being a fit for the Guardians' ideology and building goodwill with those Orders \u2014 remember also that most Awakenings fail and the Labyrinth exists as much to divert would-be questants as find them.<br /> <br /> On a more general level? Same reason powerful spirits don't just eat their inferiors \u2014 having others to take care of things for you is convenient, especially if you're trying to focus your uses of magic toward things besides basic maintenance in the name of self-definition. Even if you don't end up taking a direct hand in a new mage's development, you can hand them off to someone who will and either they or the system will compensate you for the effort. And if you <i>do</i> take them on as a student, you have unprecedented influence over their magical development and therefore a substantial ability to steer them toward or away from whatever facets of your own interests you want addressed.<br /> <br /> Errol216's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\">posts on the Mysterium's system of <i>guanxi</i></a> are somewhat helpful here as a generalizable phenomenon \u2014 favor economies inform a lot of supernatural societies by virtue of their relation to the mundane world, and understanding them is generally going to do better for constructing a setting than figuring out modes of government based on the assumption that a given locale has a whole unified institutional structure unto itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T08:06:40-07:00","id":1336557,"title":"","content":"Now, I agree some people are maybe too cynical about this. I don't think Mages are monsters. I think of them as hyper-human. For good and ill.<br /> <br /> In my current game solidarity is big among the Free Council, but I still use the guidelines for requesting favors with Order Status. It's a friendly system, people will help you out... but reciprocity is expected and there are limits. Asking someone to cast an Unmaking spell for you is still a big ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T08:37:20-07:00","id":1337327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1336104-help-with-time?p=1336111#post1336111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time travel that accomplishes anything changes the events of the past using the resources available at the time, which the basic facts of opportunity cost render as &quot;anything you tap to prevent that murder prevents it from being used the way it was used originally.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually true. There's a way around that though it's a bit of a pain in the ass, since you have to time travel twice.<br /> <br /> The Doctor spends his day playing minigolf <br /> Person A is murdered.<br /> The Doctor travels back in time and spends millions of dollars prevents the murder.<br /> Once the Doctor reaches the present and the time travel timeline becomes reality, Person A is not dead.<br /> The Doctor casts a Time Shielding on Person A to prevent time travel from affecting them.<br /> The Doctor goes back in time again, and once again spends his day playing minigolf.<br /> Person A is murdered.<br /> When the timeline reaches the point where the Time Shielding was cast, Person A is suddenly alive again.<br /> The Doctor wins his game of minigolf content with know he saved Person A's life AND only spent $8.95 for his golf game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T13:59:15-07:00","id":1337368,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that's not really going to work too well, since you'd end up Clashing of Wills against yourself as you try to alter the timeline of something you shielded from changing. Shielding someone from time-line changes isn't automatic if someone uses Time magic again to rewrite it another time. It's possible you end up undoing your own efforts instead of saving them.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible to do, but it's not reliable enough a Mage would realistically count on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T19:46:32-07:00","id":1337425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1336104-help-with-time?p=1337368#post1337368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that's not really going to work too well, since you'd end up Clashing of Wills against yourself as you try to alter the timeline of something you shielded from changing. Shielding someone from time-line changes isn't automatic if someone uses Time magic again to rewrite it another time. It's possible you end up undoing your own efforts instead of saving them.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible to do, but it's not reliable enough a Mage would realistically count on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can certainly opt to lose a CoW with yourself, just like you can choose not to contest a roll from an NPC, or choose to take a Dramatic Failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T20:02:54-07:00","id":1337431,"title":"","content":"OK, but if you fail on either side, it doesn't work. Either you fail the shield, and they die and you undid saving them, or you fail your alteration of history, and you lose your money. The idea needs both spells to operate normally, but opting to fail the CoW on either would muck with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T00:49:16-07:00","id":1337453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the mage wins, the subject is treated as though she were returning from a trip to the past herself when history settles, safeguarding her against being rewritten. </div> </div> </div><i>Constant Presence</i> only applies to the subject to which it's applied; it doesn't muck with the change in any other way. While the <u>personal timeline</u> of the protected subject should be preserved if the Clash is in its favor, it wouldn't prevent the past being rewritten, otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T03:16:02-07:00","id":1337460,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the subject's history being changed is directly relevant. Constant Presence isn't going to stop you from going back in time and buying a lottery ticket with winning numbers just because it happens to be the same point in time when you went back and stopped someone from dying.<br /> <br /> The scenario in question involves going back in time, saving someone, casting Constant Presence on them later, and then going back in time and un-saving them to recoup your material losses. That's where the CoW comes in. It only works if you try to alter their history twice, and the second is shielded. So either the alteration to the subject's history allowing you to recoup your losses wins, and the change happens (meaning the person being saved ends up dead), or Constant Presence wins, and both saving them and not saving them occur, with all the consequences there-in, but the subject survives it; so that stuff you used up in the past stays used up because that sill happens in the subject's time-line and is set once they return even if the rest of the world continued otherwise while they were &quot;gone.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T07:19:54-07:00","id":1337488,"title":"","content":"Constant Presence doesn't counter the time travel as a whole, just the changes to the subject's personal timeline. It's intended effect is breaking down causality and creating time paradoxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}